ase (LAP) contradicts CML chronic phase (LAP is characteristically low in CML)", "Acute Leukemia: No blasts in differential (normal differential) reduces likelihood", "Primary Hyperparathyroidism: No parathyroid hormone or vitamin D levels to confirm this mechanism", "Infectious/inflammatory aetiology: Normal differential and absence of localized infection signs make this secondary"], "alarm_features": ["Unexplained weight loss", "Hypercalcemia (10.9 mEq/L)", "Significant leukocytosis (66,500/mm³)", "Anemia (Hb 12 g/dL) with constitutional symptoms"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.2470701838815892, "posterior": 0.20312862357880568, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Absence of blasts in peripheral blood provides strong evidence against myeloid neoplasms with increased blasts (B1), which typically show blasts in differentia…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 3.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.051, "danger": 0.9, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.4941403677631784, "posterior": 0.40625724715761136, "danger": 0.5, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Hypercalcemia is typical of plasma cell disorders (B4) like multiple myeloma but less common in chronic myeloproliferative neoplasms (B3). This provides modera…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.6, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["chronic myeloid leukemia", "polycythemia vera", "essential thrombocythemia", "primary myelofibrosis"]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Plasma Cell Disorder", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.10634908052754355, "posterior": 0.17486968283299384, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Hypercalcemia is typical of plasma cell disorders (B4) like multiple myeloma but less common in chronic myeloproliferative neoplasms (B3). This provides modera…"], "evidence_against": ["Normal differential and lack of plasma cell markers (e.g., monoclonal protein) provide moderate evidence against multiple myeloma (B4), but hypercalcemia alone…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.75, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.165, "danger": 0.2, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "kb_myeloid_neoplasm_with_in": {"id": "kb_myeloid_neoplasm_with_in", "label": "myeloid neoplasm with increased blasts / blast crisis (AML, MDS-EB, CML-BC)", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.0, "danger": 0.0, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}}, "frontier": ["B1", "B3", "B4"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of anemia (hemogl